WEBVTT

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.670
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.960
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.520
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.770
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.370
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.680
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.960
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.090
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.960
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.940
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.710
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.140
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.650
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.880
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.080
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.680
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.920
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.300
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:35.200
<i>Currently holding at</i>
<i>an altitude of 9500!</i>

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.970
<i>Wind speed: 0.5 to 0.6.</i>

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.340
<i>Surrounding area is</i>
<i>clear of enemy presence.</i>

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.200
<i>Escort plane, stay on guard!</i>

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.110
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.670
<i>Flight program, check!</i>

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.680
<i>Linking main computer.</i>

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.720
<i>Gyro system, activated.</i>
<i>Trim control, on.</i>

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.650
<i>Generator system, R.G.A.</i>
<i>Activating all control systems.</i>

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.020
<i>How's the pressure in</i>
<i>the plasma cylinder look?</i>

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.990
<i>About 3 percent below normal.</i>

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.650
<i>It's barely within</i>
<i>the pressure limit...</i>

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.730
<i>...but I'll make it work somehow.</i>

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.700
<i>We're going to release</i>
<i>the cables now. All set?</i>

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.570
<i>Ready when you are.</i>

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.440
<i>Cable release</i>
<i>in five seconds.</i>

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:15.870
<i>Four...</i>

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.500
<i>Three...</i>

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.270
<i>Two...</i>

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.680
<i>One...</i>

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:21.740
<i>Take off!</i>

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.490
<i>9000!</i>

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>8500!</i>

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.420
<i>8000!</i>

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.420
<i>7500!</i>

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.320
<i>7000!</i>

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.970
<i>6500!</i>

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.700
<i>6000!</i>

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>Minovsky particle compressor</i>
<i>functioning normally!</i>

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.910
<i>Plasma propulsion power</i>
<i>is at point zero.</i>

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.680
<i>Within predicted values.</i>

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.850
<i>No instability detected</i>
<i>in gyro system.</i>

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.890
The vibration's less
than I was expecting.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.290
I'm increasing power.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.010
So, this... This is
Big Brother's dream.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.530
Hey, check it out!
The Reaper's hard at work!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.800
Oh? I feel sorry
for poor Karen.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.670
Gettin' stuck with
a jinx like him!

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.640
No kidding! I pity them.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.410
What are those
guys talking about?

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.320
Does it not bother
him any more...

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.680
...after all those other
teammates of his he's killed?

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:05.120
That newbie commander of his
is probably dead meat, too.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.420
S- Sir!

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.020
Betcha he'll haunt him
forever after he dies...

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.160
Sir, please!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.200
You son of a bitch!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.100
Now you've done it, Reaper!

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.730
Trouble!

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.960
Commander! Commander!

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.240
Oh, for God's sake!
Commander, where are you?!

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.670
The Reaper's fighting someone?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.680
- Who's he fighting?!
- The guys from the 07th Team!

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.590
Get your bets in!
Hurry up, before it's over!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.490
Where's the fight?!

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.590
380 meters away
at 10 o'clock!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.260
But, sir, is it true that...

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.630
...everyone who's fought with
him so far is dead now?!

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.630
Who told you a stupid
thing like that?!

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:59.370
Hey, you guys fight fair!

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:04.010
Okay, Reaper, now it's
time to rest in peace!

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.920
Let me through!
C'mon, let me through!

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.740
Three against one?!

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.150
You guys aren't
even fighting fair!

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.250
Who's next?!

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:25.990
Just what the hell are
you people doing?!

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.160
Sir! Recreation, sir!

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.710
It was a deep exchange
between fellow MS Teams, sir!

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.680
An "exchange," huh?
In this god damned heat?!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.970
Whatever. 07th Team!

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.380
Aren't you on rear line support in that
area to the west we just opened up?

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.510
Sir! We'll leave right away!

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:46.250
Right. And 08th Team...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.380
...I want you ready to
move on a moment's notice.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.480
Sir!

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.560
Both of you! Dismissed!

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.460
Sir!

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.190
And the rest of you get
back to where you belong.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:59.830
And I'll just keep
this for myself...

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:05.760
Well, just keep your distance
from the Reaper, Newbie.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.980
It's just stupid trash-talk.
Don't let it bother you.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.340
Yes, sir...

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.110
Let's go!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.660
Thanks to all of your efforts,
the Apsalus Project...

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.290
...has successfully completed
its first stage.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.000
The day of the Apsalus's
completion is near!

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.440
With its completion, our power over
the Earth system shall be renewed...

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.840
...and then the light of victory
will surely fall upon Zeon!

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.040
Glory to Zeon!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:52.380
Sieg Zeon! Sieg Zeon!
Sieg Zeon! Sieg Zeon!

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:03.660
That's why Duke Degwin placed me
in personal charge of this project.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.470
Oh, Aina! You look lovelier
than ever this evening!

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.840
Big Brother...

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:25.080
Your test flight today
was a great feat.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:29.280
I've run out of words to
describe how wonderful it felt.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:32.950
Except the air conditioning
still needs some work.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.000
I was sweating in there.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:42.190
Although that made the drink
I got later taste even better.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.700
You did very well. Now take
this evening to enjoy yourself.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.570
Ginias!

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.700
Where's Ginias?!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.720
Admiral Yuri Kellanay.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.480
Outta my way! Lemme through!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.980
Hey there!

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.860
Ginias! Long time, no see!

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:07.160
Would you stop it?
People are staring.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.960
Aw, what the hell
does that matter?

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.500
I heard you got your
high-priced toy built...

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.660
...and came running over
here from Europe to see it.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.100
A "toy"?!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.300
Oh! Aina!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.200
My God, I'm just speechless!

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.340
This lovely lady is
really little Aina?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.640
Last time I saw you,
you were still just a kid.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.880
Women really know
how to surprise you...

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.320
You've also turned out
very well, Mr. Kellanay.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.450
Whoa, whoa!
Quit being so formal!

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.760
It's not like we're
strangers or anything.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.700
Aina...

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.500
Come on.
Say you'll be my girl.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:51.730
Why stick around some guy...

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.210
...who only cares about
preserving the Sahalin name...

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:56.640
...when you can come with
me and have some fun?

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.440
You must be joking.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.210
The air in here suddenly
doesn't agree with me.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.620
I think I need to step outside.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.280
If you'll excuse me!

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.830
Never lets her guard down,
does she? Right?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.760
Those two are no fun!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:32.050
Now, of all times,
he shows up!

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:36.020
Whenever he shows up, he throws
off Big Brother's normal rhythms.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:40.050
If I were Ginias, I'd have
punched that guy out!

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.520
Miss Aina!

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.150
Miss Aina,
why did you come here?

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.290
For Big Brother's dream...

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.330
Does saying that
sound strange?

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.370
No.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:55.700
Once his Apsalus is completed,
this war will finally end.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.470
Although a lot of people...

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.670
...are going to lose their
lives to a weapon like that...

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.710
It's for the sake of
the Sahalin family.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:07.470
My existence will be linked
with that of your family's...

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:08.850
...as it has always been.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.680
Thank you, Norris.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:14.480
Honor and glory... And lineage.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.150
I'm part of the Sahalin family.
It's like being a puppet.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.560
Miss Aina...

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:36.940
What's wrong, Sanders?

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:41.710
I'm... quitting being
a mobile suit pilot.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.140
I'm requesting a transfer.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.780
You're what?!

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:48.050
Eledore, take my place.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.890
Wh- What are you talking
about?! I can't do that...

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:56.050
Oh, well, you think
I should pilot it?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.790
What's this all about?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.390
I can't go out there.
Not as a pilot.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.460
I don't want you
all getting killed!

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.410
You stupid!

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.140
Karen!

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.180
You're still saying
that bullshit?!

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.810
Okay, yeah. You've lost every
team you've fought with so far!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:20.490
But you let what those jerks in
the 07th Team said get to you...

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.080
...and now you believe you
really are the Grim Reaper!

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:26.950
Th- That's why I...

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:29.160
You think quitting'll
make you feel better?!

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.490
Only if you don't
have any balls!

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.430
So you do have
some down there.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.840
Hey! Karen!

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.600
The team would be better off...

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.840
...without a god damned
coward like you on it!

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.240
That's enough!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.510
Stop it right there,
Master Chief!

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.210
But...

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.980
No, it's all right.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.080
All the other teams
I've served with...

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:57.220
...have been wiped out
on their third mission.

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.590
All except me.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:02.560
A third-time jinx?

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:07.860
As long as I'm in it, the 08th
Team is doomed to die.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.970
That's why I want to quit!

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.860
Isn't thinking that it's your
fault your friends got killed...

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.880
...just a LITTLE
bit conceited?

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:18.470
Who do you think you are?!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.520
Can't you get that
through your head?!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.880
We're in the
middle of a mission.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.450
Sanders, I can't accept
your transfer out here.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.420
Now get back to your post.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.730
But...

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.460
That's an order.

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.130
Right...

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:45.070
Don't worry. We'll be the ones
who cure you of this crazy idea.

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:52.100
Christ, now these lousy
rations taste even worse.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:57.910
Hey, Commander, I hope we don't
see any action tomorrow, either.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.780
Christ...

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.420
If you want to survive,
you have to trust each other.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.960
You have to have faith.

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.220
A warning alarm!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.420
I can see that.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.930
We may be at its limit. The telemeter
is also acting strangely.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.730
I don't think so.
Contact all units...

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.060
...and have them form as strong
a defense line as possible!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.100
I want the Apsalus's
flight path secured!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.790
<i>Norris! Give me a report on</i>
<i>the condition of the unit's body.</i>

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:53.070
<i>Yes, sir. I see no apparent</i>
<i>changes at the moment.</i>

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.270
<i>All right. Continue</i>
<i>monitoring the load rate.</i>

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.210
Aye.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.580
<i>Miss Aina, you shouldn't</i>
<i>push it too hard.</i>

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.480
I know that.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:12.290
Dammit, what are
they trying to do?

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.630
Sanders, we're going to
move into Area 376.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.800
<i>You read me?</i>
<i>I'm taking point.</i>

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.230
<i>Now follow me!</i>

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.630
Aye...

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.240
I've got a bad
feeling about this.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:31.740
What are you doing?

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:34.580
- Writing my will.
- You do that!

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.080
I'm getting another strong
vibration through the main body.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.350
Current altitude: 4000!
The load's too high!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.490
<i>I can't maintain this attitude.</i>
<i>Going into a dive!</i>

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.560
<i>Try to override the code</i>
<i>in the control computer!</i>

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.190
<i>We're inside of Feddie-</i>
<i>controlled territory.</i>

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:54.500
<i>Be careful!</i>

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.230
I can't climb!

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:59.870
<i>I know you can do this!</i>
<i>Just stop its descent!</i>

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.430
Aye.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:03.340
Broadcast Minovsky particles!

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.640
We'll increase altitude and
maintain contact with the base.

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:06.340
<i>Please!</i>

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.160
Is the north-east defense
line moving up?

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.100
Yes, sir. They're initiating
a diversion attack.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.130
Hey, Ginias! Enough already!

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.530
Have Aina punch out
of that thing!

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.730
We can't afford to
lose the Apsalus!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.770
I know Aina can handle this.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.830
<i>This is escort unit.</i>

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.280
<i>Looks like she managed to</i>
<i>stop falling just in time.</i>

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:42.050
Well done, Aina! Send out the
reserve troops as well!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.280
We have to keep the Feddies' eyes
off of the Apsalus's flight path!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:46.640
Sir!

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.920
Christ, it's hard
to clean up things...

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.580
...when you brains get
overconfident, right?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.550
Sir...

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.590
<i>We have partially</i>
<i>regained attitude control!</i>

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.400
<i>Detecting power system overheat!</i>

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:02.930
It's time for me to head
back to the European front.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.600
Once you work out the bugs on
that thing, send it over to me.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:10.240
I didn't build it
for the likes of you.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.470
I hear you, Mr. Genius.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:20.150
<i>Eledore! Can you find</i>
<i>the enemy for me?</i>

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:24.320
<i>2000 meters away at 11 o'clock!</i>
<i>Karen's currently pursuing them.</i>

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:33.060
What's going on here?

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.300
Commander!
The enemy's pulling back!

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.130
<i>Like he WANTS us to follow him.</i>

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.900
Strange...
Something's going on here.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.910
Wh- What the hell is that?!

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:48.950
What's wrong?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.140
Quiet!

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.310
<i>What do we do, Commander?</i>
<i>Do we follow them?</i>

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:54.220
<i>No. Hold on.</i>

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.550
Something's around here...

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.590
<i>Commander! Listen to this!</i>

00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:00.350
<i>...about 25 klicks to</i>
<i>the east. Recover it!</i>

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.690
<i>Roger. We should reach</i>
<i>the Apsalus soon.</i>

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.100
<i>It's somewhere in the jungle.</i>

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.660
<i>Hurry up and secure</i>
<i>the Apsalus's flight path.</i>

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.630
What the hell?

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.110
<i>I can barely hear it because</i>
<i>of Minovsky particle jamming...</i>

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.240
<i>...but I think some sort of</i>
<i>enemy unit is headed this way.</i>

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:23.010
<i>But why isn't this in code?</i>

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:27.050
All right! We'll stay
here and wait for it!

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.220
All units, lay low!

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.930
You really think
it's coming this way?

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.700
It's definitely coming!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:46.140
Commander! It'll be over
your head in 40 seconds!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.040
<i>Gotcha. We'll let them pass</i>
<i>and see what happens.</i>

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.710
- You think this is Sanders' fault?
- Just shut up!

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.780
I'm picking up a pressure vibration.

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:02.380
<i>This thing's pretty big!</i>
<i>Way bigger than a mobile suit!</i>

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.390
<i>Fighter plane engines.</i>
<i>Multiple contacts.</i>

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.700
Here they come!

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:20.500
Let them pass.

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.670
Who's shooting?!

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:26.240
<i>Concentrate on that</i>
<i>point of fire!</i>

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.680
<i>Secure the Apsalus's</i>
<i>flight path!</i>

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.550
<i>Roger!</i>

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.180
You dumb ass!
Why'd you fire at them?!

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.490
Wh- What'll we do?!

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.860
<i>They're coming right</i>
<i>for us! Scatter!</i>

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.530
What'd he do that for?!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.840
<i>You read me, Sanders?</i>

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:52.170
<i>I'm not gonna die!</i>
<i>Just watch me!</i>

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.240
<i>Karen! What the hell</i>
<i>are you doing?!</i>

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.780
There! Did you see that...

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:06.850
Karen!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:15.460
Karen!

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.930
It... It's huge!

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.700
What is this thing?

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.290
Did I get him?!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.330
Norris!

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:57.970
<i>Forgive me, Miss Aina!</i>

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.970
Can you make it
back to the base?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:03.770
<i>I'll be all right! Please,</i>
<i>Miss Aina, get out of here!</i>

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.400
No! I'll cover you!

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:07.950
<i>You get out of here</i>
<i>in the meantime!</i>

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:08.850
<i>Miss Aina!</i>

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.890
If you're coming,
then come on!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.600
YOU GOD DAMNED MONSTER!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.240
They're not going to die!

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.300
I won't let any of them die!

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.380
You like that?!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.730
He's insane!

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:12.080
I am not... I am not...
I AM NOT THE GRIM REAPER!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:27.390
I won't lose! I won't lose!
I'm not going to lose!

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:34.560
Shoot! Keep shooting!

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.540
Keep shooting till
your guns overheat!

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:41.740
<i>Miss Aina! It's too risky to</i>
<i>stay that close to them!</i>

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:43.540
<i>Get out of there now!</i>

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:44.540
R- Right!

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.860
<i>Sanders, you were great!</i>

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:11.300
See, Chief? I'm still alive!

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.810
Yeah... Still alive.

00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:19.910
We... We're all right!

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.920
Yeah, looks that way.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:25.040
Of course we are!

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.710
You can break any jinx.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:30.770
As long as you have faith.

00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.800
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:57.490
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:01.630
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:05.400
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:08.570
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.580
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:16.710
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:19.850
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:20.530 --> 00:23:22.990
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:27.860
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:33.730
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:38.070
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:42.970
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:46.740
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:53.880
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.990
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:58.060 --> 00:24:02.060
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:05.800
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:12.490
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.300
The existence of
the new Zeon weapon...

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:21.210
...sends a shock
through our forces.

00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:23.770
Even the 08th Team
is sent out every day...

00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:25.900
...for search and
intelligence gathering.

00:24:26.410 --> 00:24:28.680
Amidst all this, we get word that...

00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:31.310
...Eledore and Michel have
been captured by the Zeon!

00:24:31.390 --> 00:24:32.910
I hope those two
will be all right!

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:34.610
We'll save you,
no matter what!

00:24:34.820 --> 00:24:39.490
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:40.300 --> 00:24:42.320
"The Broken Order to Stand By."
